      "text": "History of the Node js :::::\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "History of the Node js :::::\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JYu-E4zpM42rPBXOxx3sp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 230.41195894150246,
      "y": 670.9098466884539,
      "width": 1430.9706727293042,
      "height": 2100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#da77f2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1471536546,
      "version": 79,
      "versionNonce": 671431102,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789462629190,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Backend actually kab aaya?\n\nBackend ka concept Node.js ya web ke saath start nahi hua. Client-server computing mein server pehle se hi exist karta tha. Client request\nbhejta tha aur server data/process karke response deta tha.\n\nWeb ke early days, especially 1990s ke beginning mein, websites mostly static HTML pages hoti thi. Web server bas requested HTML file browser ko\nreturn karta tha. Ismein user ke according dynamic data ya complex business logic nahi hota tha.\n\n2. Dynamic websites ki need kyu aayi?\n\nJaise-jaise websites useful applications banne lagi—login, registration, shopping, user accounts, search, database-driven content—sirf static HTML\nenough nahi tha.\n\nServer ko request receive karke:\n\nuser ko identify karna,\ndatabase se data nikalna,\nbusiness logic execute karna,\naur dynamically response generate karna\n\npadta tha.\n\nYahin modern web backend ka importance badha.\n\n3. CGI kyu aaya?\n\n1990s mein CGI (Common Gateway Interface) ne web server ko external programs ke saath communicate karne ka standard way diya.\n\nIsse developer server-side program likh sakta tha jo request process karta, database se data laata aur dynamic HTML generate karta.\n\nCGI ne static web ki limitation solve kar di.\n\nLekin CGI ka ek major drawback tha: traditional CGI model mein requests handle karne ke liye separate processes create karna expensive ho\nsakta tha. Traffic badhne par process creation aur memory/CPU overhead problem ban sakta tha.\n\n4. CGI ke baad kya hua?\n\nWeb applications increasingly complex aur high-traffic hone lagi. Isliye PHP, Java Servlets/JSP, ASP.NET, Python, Ruby jaise server-side\ntechnologies aur application frameworks popular hue.\n\nIn technologies ne developers ko better application structure, reusable code, database integration, sessions, authentication aur business logic\nhandle karne ke better mechanisms diye.\n\nYaani CGI ko simply \"replace\" nahi kiya gaya; server-side development ka model progressively more sophisticated hota gaya.\n\n5. Phir web ka nature change hua\n\n2000s mein web pages increasingly interactive hone lage. Browser mein JavaScript ka use badha aur AJAX jaise approaches popular hue.\n\nAb har interaction par complete HTML page reload karna zaroori nahi tha. Browser background mein server ko request bhej sakta tha aur server\nse sirf required data receive kar sakta tha.\n\nIsse API-based backend ka importance badhne laga.\n\nBackend ka kaam sirf HTML generate karna nahi raha. Woh increasingly data aur services provide karne wala API layer banne laga.\n\n6. Yahan Node.js kyu aaya?\n\n2009 mein Ryan Dahl ne Node.js introduce kiya.\n\nNode.js ka major change ye tha ki JavaScript ko browser ke bahar server-side run karna possible hua.\n\nIsse JavaScript sirf frontend language nahi rahi; developers JavaScript ka use karke backend services aur APIs bhi bana sakte the.\n\nLekin Node.js ka sirf JavaScript server par chalna hi important nahi tha.\n\nNode.js ne event-driven, non-blocking I/O model provide kiya, jo especially network aur database jaise I/O operations wali applications mein large\nnumbers of concurrent requests handle karne ke liye attractive tha.\n\n7. Node.js ne purani technologies ko replace kyu nahi kiya?\n\nYe bahut important hai.\n\nNode.js PHP, Java, Python ya .NET ka replacement nahi tha.\n\nHar technology ke apne advantages hain. Node.js ek additional backend runtime bana.\n\nNode.js particularly un situations mein attractive hua jahan:\n\nbahut network requests hoti hain,\ndatabase/API calls zyada hoti hain,\nreal-time communication chahiye,\nlightweight APIs/services banani hain,\nfrontend aur backend dono mein JavaScript ecosystem use karna convenient hai.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Backend actually kab aaya?\n\nBackend ka concept Node.js ya web ke saath start nahi hua. Client-server computing mein server pehle se hi exist karta tha. Client request bhejta tha aur server data/process karke response deta tha.\n\nWeb ke early days, especially 1990s ke beginning mein, websites mostly static HTML pages hoti thi. Web server bas requested HTML file browser ko return karta tha. Ismein user ke according dynamic data ya complex business logic nahi hota tha.\n\n2. Dynamic websites ki need kyu aayi?\n\nJaise-jaise websites useful applications banne lagi—login, registration, shopping, user accounts, search, database-driven content—sirf static HTML enough nahi tha.\n\nServer ko request receive karke:\n\nuser ko identify karna,\ndatabase se data nikalna,\nbusiness logic execute karna,\naur dynamically response generate karna\n\npadta tha.\n\nYahin modern web backend ka importance badha.\n\n3. CGI kyu aaya?\n\n1990s mein CGI (Common Gateway Interface) ne web server ko external programs ke saath communicate karne ka standard way diya.\n\nIsse developer server-side program likh sakta tha jo request process karta, database se data laata aur dynamic HTML generate karta.\n\nCGI ne static web ki limitation solve kar di.\n\nLekin CGI ka ek major drawback tha: traditional CGI model mein requests handle karne ke liye separate processes create karna expensive ho sakta tha. Traffic badhne par process creation aur memory/CPU overhead problem ban sakta tha.\n\n4. CGI ke baad kya hua?\n\nWeb applications increasingly complex aur high-traffic hone lagi. Isliye PHP, Java Servlets/JSP, ASP.NET, Python, Ruby jaise server-side technologies aur application frameworks popular hue.\n\nIn technologies ne developers ko better application structure, reusable code, database integration, sessions, authentication aur business logic handle karne ke better mechanisms diye.\n\nYaani CGI ko simply \"replace\" nahi kiya gaya; server-side development ka model progressively more sophisticated hota gaya.\n\n5. Phir web ka nature change hua\n\n2000s mein web pages increasingly interactive hone lage. Browser mein JavaScript ka use badha aur AJAX jaise approaches popular hue.\n\nAb har interaction par complete HTML page reload karna zaroori nahi tha. Browser background mein server ko request bhej sakta tha aur server se sirf required data receive kar sakta tha.\n\nIsse API-based backend ka importance badhne laga.\n\nBackend ka kaam sirf HTML generate karna nahi raha. Woh increasingly data aur services provide karne wala API layer banne laga.\n\n6. Yahan Node.js kyu aaya?\n\n2009 mein Ryan Dahl ne Node.js introduce kiya.\n\nNode.js ka major change ye tha ki JavaScript ko browser ke bahar server-side run karna possible hua.\n\nIsse JavaScript sirf frontend language nahi rahi; developers JavaScript ka use karke backend services aur APIs bhi bana sakte the.\n\nLekin Node.js ka sirf JavaScript server par chalna hi important nahi tha.\n\nNode.js ne event-driven, non-blocking I/O model provide kiya, jo especially network aur database jaise I/O operations wali applications mein large numbers of concurrent requests handle karne ke liye attractive tha.\n\n7. Node.js ne purani technologies ko replace kyu nahi kiya?\n\nYe bahut important hai.\n\nNode.js PHP, Java, Python ya .NET ka replacement nahi tha.\n\nHar technology ke apne advantages hain. Node.js ek additional backend runtime bana.\n\nNode.js particularly un situations mein attractive hua jahan:\n\nbahut network requests hoti hain,\ndatabase/API calls zyada hoti hain,\nreal-time communication chahiye,\nlightweight APIs/services banani hain,\nfrontend aur backend dono mein JavaScript ecosystem use karna convenient hai.",
