      "seed": 1650137854,
      "version": 39,
      "versionNonce": 1975664482,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789463729270,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Single-Threaded Architecture — Node.js\n1. What?\nSingle-threaded ka matlab hai ki Node.js ka main JavaScript execution ek single thread par hota hai.\nIs main thread ko primarily Event Loop ke through manage kiya jata hai.\nEk time par JavaScript code ka ek piece of work execute hota hai.\n2. Problem kya thi?\n\nTraditional server models mein har request ko handle karne ke liye multiple threads/processes use kiye ja sakte the.\n\nHigh traffic par:\n\nbahut threads create ho sakte hain\nmemory usage badh sakta hai\nthread management ka overhead hota hai\ncontext switching ka cost hota hai\n3. Node.js ne kya approach li?\n\nNode.js ne JavaScript execution ke liye single main thread + Event Loop approach use ki.\n\nIska goal tha:\n\nHar request ke liye ek naya JavaScript thread create karne ke bajay, ek main thread se efficiently multiple requests manage karna.\n\n4. Important: Single-threaded ka matlab kya Nahi hai?\n\nYe mat samajhna:\n\n❌ \"Node.js mein sirf ek hi thread hota hai.\"\n\nActually Node.js process ke andar underlying system/runtime kuch operations ke liye additional threads use kar sakta hai.\n\nImportant distinction:\n\nJavaScript execution → main thread\nCertain background operations → runtime/OS/thread pool etc.\n\n5. I/O ke case mein iska benefit\n\nSuppose database operation mein time lag raha hai.\n\nNode.js main JavaScript thread ko unnecessarily wait karane ke bajay I/O operation initiate karke dusre work ko process kar sakta hai.\n\nJab I/O complete hota hai, uska result event loop ke through JavaScript execution ke liye handle hota hai.\n\n6. Main benefit\n\nSingle main JavaScript thread + non-blocking I/O + Event Loop\n\n→ fewer threads needed for typical I/O-heavy workloads\n→ efficient handling of many concurrent I/O operations\n→ simpler JavaScript concurrency model\n\n7. Limitation\n\nSingle main thread ka matlab ye bhi hai ki agar tum CPU-heavy JavaScript operation chala do:\n\nHeavy calculation\nLarge loop\nComplex computation\n\ntoh main thread busy ho sakta hai.\n\nResult:\n\nEvent Loop block → doosri requests delay\n\nIsliye Node.js I/O-heavy workloads ke liye particularly strong hai, jabki CPU-heavy work ko carefully handle karna padta hai (e.g. worker threads/processes).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Single-Threaded Architecture — Node.js\n1. What?\nSingle-threaded ka matlab hai ki Node.js ka main JavaScript execution ek single thread par hota hai.\nIs main thread ko primarily Event Loop ke through manage kiya jata hai.\nEk time par JavaScript code ka ek piece of work execute hota hai.\n2. Problem kya thi?\n\nTraditional server models mein har request ko handle karne ke liye multiple threads/processes use kiye ja sakte the.\n\nHigh traffic par:\n\nbahut threads create ho sakte hain\nmemory usage badh sakta hai\nthread management ka overhead hota hai\ncontext switching ka cost hota hai\n3. Node.js ne kya approach li?\n\nNode.js ne JavaScript execution ke liye single main thread + Event Loop approach use ki.\n\nIska goal tha:\n\nHar request ke liye ek naya JavaScript thread create karne ke bajay, ek main thread se efficiently multiple requests manage karna.\n\n4. Important: Single-threaded ka matlab kya Nahi hai?\n\nYe mat samajhna:\n\n❌ \"Node.js mein sirf ek hi thread hota hai.\"\n\nActually Node.js process ke andar underlying system/runtime kuch operations ke liye additional threads use kar sakta hai.\n\nImportant distinction:\n\nJavaScript execution → main thread\nCertain background operations → runtime/OS/thread pool etc.\n\n5. I/O ke case mein iska benefit\n\nSuppose database operation mein time lag raha hai.\n\nNode.js main JavaScript thread ko unnecessarily wait karane ke bajay I/O operation initiate karke dusre work ko process kar sakta hai.\n\nJab I/O complete hota hai, uska result event loop ke through JavaScript execution ke liye handle hota hai.\n\n6. Main benefit\n\nSingle main JavaScript thread + non-blocking I/O + Event Loop\n\n→ fewer threads needed for typical I/O-heavy workloads\n→ efficient handling of many concurrent I/O operations\n→ simpler JavaScript concurrency model\n\n7. Limitation\n\nSingle main thread ka matlab ye bhi hai ki agar tum CPU-heavy JavaScript operation chala do:\n\nHeavy calculation\nLarge loop\nComplex computation\n\ntoh main thread busy ho sakta hai.\n\nResult:\n\nEvent Loop block → doosri requests delay\n\nIsliye Node.js I/O-heavy workloads ke liye particularly strong hai, jabki CPU-heavy work ko carefully handle karna padta hai (e.g. worker threads/processes).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
