    {
      "id": "Gt-qw4mxvQTX5fxloNOWj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -240.62248848575268,
      "y": 12323.909146310838,
      "width": 1542.339111328125,
      "height": 1150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#3bc9db",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 911841086,
      "version": 10,
      "versionNonce": 324485410,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789465289582,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. What is Thread Pool?\n\nThread Pool kuch pre-existing/background threads ka group hota hai jo certain tasks ko main JavaScript thread ke bahar execute karne ke liye use hota hai.\n\nNode.js mein libuv thread pool provide karti hai.\n\n2. Kyu use hota hai?\n\nKuch operations naturally asynchronous nahi hote ya unhe background mein execute karna better hota hai.\n\nAgar aise operation ko main JavaScript thread par directly perform kiya jaye:\n\nMain thread block ho sakta hai → Event Loop slow ho sakta hai.\n\nThread Pool in supported operations ko background threads par handle karne mein help karta hai.\n\n3. Common examples\n\nNode.js mein thread pool commonly certain:\n\nFile System operations\nDNS operations \nCryptographic operations\nCompression operations\n\nke liye use ho sakta hai.\n\n4. Main benefit\n\nMain JavaScript thread ko blocking work se free rakhna, taaki Event Loop doosre tasks handle kar sake.\n\n5. Important clarification\n\nThread Pool ≠ Event Loop\n\nEvent Loop → callbacks/async work ko coordinate karta hai.\nThread Pool → kuch specific operations ko background threads par execute karta hai.\n🔥 Main points\n\nThread Pool = background threads ka group\n\nProvided by = libuv\n\nPurpose = certain blocking/heavy operations ko main JS thread se bahar handle karna\n\nBenefit = Event Loop ko unnecessarily block hone se bachana ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. What is Thread Pool?\n\nThread Pool kuch pre-existing/background threads ka group hota hai jo certain tasks ko main JavaScript thread ke bahar execute karne ke liye use hota hai.\n\nNode.js mein libuv thread pool provide karti hai.\n\n2. Kyu use hota hai?\n\nKuch operations naturally asynchronous nahi hote ya unhe background mein execute karna better hota hai.\n\nAgar aise operation ko main JavaScript thread par directly perform kiya jaye:\n\nMain thread block ho sakta hai → Event Loop slow ho sakta hai.\n\nThread Pool in supported operations ko background threads par handle karne mein help karta hai.\n\n3. Common examples\n\nNode.js mein thread pool commonly certain:\n\nFile System operations\nDNS operations \nCryptographic operations\nCompression operations\n\nke liye use ho sakta hai.\n\n4. Main benefit\n\nMain JavaScript thread ko blocking work se free rakhna, taaki Event Loop doosre tasks handle kar sake.\n\n5. Important clarification\n\nThread Pool ≠ Event Loop\n\nEvent Loop → callbacks/async work ko coordinate karta hai.\nThread Pool → kuch specific operations ko background threads par execute karta hai.\n🔥 Main points\n\nThread Pool = background threads ka group\n\nProvided by = libuv\n\nPurpose = certain blocking/heavy operations ko main JS thread se bahar handle karna\n\nBenefit = Event Loop ko unnecessarily block hone se bachana ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
