    },
    {
      "id": "9LdYHVr-snEQptd8WgFAW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2498.4800567626953,
      "y": 371.1666107177797,
      "width": 1397.37548828125,
      "height": 4320,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 678920263,
      "version": 72,
      "versionNonce": 504047177,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789817788692,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Environment Variable\nWhat: App ki configuration value.\nWhy: Configuration code ke bahar rakhni hai.\nSolves: Hard-coded configuration.\n\n\n2. .env\nWhat: Variables store karne wali file.\nWhy: Configuration ek jagah rakhni hai.\nSolves: Code mein values directly likhne ki problem.\n\n3. dotenv\nWhat: .env read karne wala package.\nWhy: .env ki values application mein load karni hain.\nSolves: .env values ko manually load karne ki problem.\n\n\n4. dotenv.config()\nWhat: .env values load karta hai.\nWhy: Values ko application ke andar available karna.\nSolves: Environment variables unavailable hone ki problem.\n\n5. process.env\nWhat: Environment variables access karne ka interface.\nWhy: Loaded values ko code mein use karna.\nSolves: Configuration values access karne ki problem.\n\n\n6. NODE_ENV\nWhat: Current environment identify karta hai.\nWhy: Development/production distinguish karna.\nSolves: Environment identify karne ki problem.\n\n\n7. .env.local\nWhat: Development configuration file.\nWhy: Local settings alag rakhni hain.\nSolves: Development settings ko production se mix hone se bachata hai.\n\n8. .env.production\nWhat: Production configuration file.\nWhy: Live application ki settings alag rakhni hain.\nSolves: Production configuration ko development se separate karta hai.\n\n\n9. Development vs Production\nWhat: Do different environments.\nWhy: Testing aur live application separate rakhni hai.\nSolves: Development testing se production data affect hone ka risk.]\n\n\n10. cross-env\nWhat: Command ke time environment variable set karta hai.\nWhy: NODE_ENV easily set karna.\nSolves: Different OS par environment variable set karne ki compatibility problem.\n\n11. path\nWhat: Node.js built-in path module.\nWhy: File paths handle karne hain.\nSolves: File path manually construct karne ki problem.\n\n\n12. process.cwd()\nWhat: Current working directory deta hai.\nWhy: Project ka current location pata karna.\nSolves: Current project folder identify karne ki problem.\n\n\n13. path.resolve()\nWhat: Complete/absolute path banata hai.\nWhy: .env file ka exact path banana.\nSolves: File location/path ambiguity.\n\n\n14. Environment Selection\nWhat: NODE_ENV ke basis par .env select karna.\nWhy: Correct environment ki settings load karni hain.\nSolves: Manually .env file change karne ki problem.\n\n\n15. Main Advantage\nWhat: Same code, different configuration.\nWhy: Local aur production easily manage karna.\nSolves: Har environment ke liye code modify karne ki problem.\n\n\n16. Security\nWhat: Secrets configuration mein rakhna.\nWhy: Passwords/API keys code se separate rakhni hain.\nSolves: Secrets accidentally code/GitHub mein expose hone ka risk.\n\n\n17. .env.example\nWhat: Required variables ka template.\nWhy: Team ko required configuration batani hai.\nSolves: New developer ko required environment variables samajhne ki problem.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Environment Variable\nWhat: App ki configuration value.\nWhy: Configuration code ke bahar rakhni hai.\nSolves: Hard-coded configuration.\n\n\n2. .env\nWhat: Variables store karne wali file.\nWhy: Configuration ek jagah rakhni hai.\nSolves: Code mein values directly likhne ki problem.\n\n3. dotenv\nWhat: .env read karne wala package.\nWhy: .env ki values application mein load karni hain.\nSolves: .env values ko manually load karne ki problem.\n\n\n4. dotenv.config()\nWhat: .env values load karta hai.\nWhy: Values ko application ke andar available karna.\nSolves: Environment variables unavailable hone ki problem.\n\n5. process.env\nWhat: Environment variables access karne ka interface.\nWhy: Loaded values ko code mein use karna.\nSolves: Configuration values access karne ki problem.\n\n\n6. NODE_ENV\nWhat: Current environment identify karta hai.\nWhy: Development/production distinguish karna.\nSolves: Environment identify karne ki problem.\n\n\n7. .env.local\nWhat: Development configuration file.\nWhy: Local settings alag rakhni hain.\nSolves: Development settings ko production se mix hone se bachata hai.\n\n8. .env.production\nWhat: Production configuration file.\nWhy: Live application ki settings alag rakhni hain.\nSolves: Production configuration ko development se separate karta hai.\n\n\n9. Development vs Production\nWhat: Do different environments.\nWhy: Testing aur live application separate rakhni hai.\nSolves: Development testing se production data affect hone ka risk.]\n\n\n10. cross-env\nWhat: Command ke time environment variable set karta hai.\nWhy: NODE_ENV easily set karna.\nSolves: Different OS par environment variable set karne ki compatibility problem.\n\n11. path\nWhat: Node.js built-in path module.\nWhy: File paths handle karne hain.\nSolves: File path manually construct karne ki problem.\n\n\n12. process.cwd()\nWhat: Current working directory deta hai.\nWhy: Project ka current location pata karna.\nSolves: Current project folder identify karne ki problem.\n\n\n13. path.resolve()\nWhat: Complete/absolute path banata hai.\nWhy: .env file ka exact path banana.\nSolves: File location/path ambiguity.\n\n\n14. Environment Selection\nWhat: NODE_ENV ke basis par .env select karna.\nWhy: Correct environment ki settings load karni hain.\nSolves: Manually .env file change karne ki problem.\n\n\n15. Main Advantage\nWhat: Same code, different configuration.\nWhy: Local aur production easily manage karna.\nSolves: Har environment ke liye code modify karne ki problem.\n\n\n16. Security\nWhat: Secrets configuration mein rakhna.\nWhy: Passwords/API keys code se separate rakhni hain.\nSolves: Secrets accidentally code/GitHub mein expose hone ka risk.\n\n\n17. .env.example\nWhat: Required variables ka template.\nWhy: Team ko required configuration batani hai.\nSolves: New developer ko required environment variables samajhne ki problem.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
