      "updated": 1790083830815,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "const express = require(\"express\") — Ye line sirf itna karti hai ki 'express' naam ki library (jo already npm install se\naayi thi) ko apni file mein le aate ho. Is step mein kuch banta nahi, bas ek function tumhare paas available ho jaata\nhai, jiska naam 'express' hai.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "const express = require(\"express\") — Ye line sirf itna karti hai ki 'express' naam ki library (jo already npm install se aayi thi) ko apni file mein le aate ho. Is step mein kuch banta nahi, bas ek function tumhare paas available ho jaata hai, jiska naam 'express' hai.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yGiLNtf-bgrb2MZ1X0qgS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4540.093663896834,
      "y": 4450.090560222118,
      "width": 1756.341796875,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b11",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1642372363,
      "version": 205,
      "versionNonce": 1899667781,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790083884441,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Call karna — us function ko chalanaconst app = express() — Yahan tum us 'express' function ko () lagake call kar\nrahe ho, matlab 'chalao ise'. Jaise hi ye chalega, ye ek naya object banayega aur wapas (return) kar dega. Wo\nreturn hua object turant 'app' variable mein store ho jaata hai.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Call karna — us function ko chalanaconst app = express() — Yahan tum us 'express' function ko () lagake call kar rahe ho, matlab 'chalao ise'. Jaise hi ye chalega, ye ek naya object banayega aur wapas (return) kar dega. Wo return hua object turant 'app' variable mein store ho jaata hai.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3f24PvLJgDZRr4mSEMUa7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4528.086115882511,
      "y": 4853.492804438985,
      "width": 1617.5640869140625,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b12",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 782029829,
      "version": 93,
      "versionNonce": 1921001131,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790083920046,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Use karna — app object se kaam lenaapp.get(...), app.listen(...) — Ab jo object mila (app), uske andar\npehle se functions maujood hain. Tum bas dot (.) lagake unko bulaate ho — jaise app.get() se route banate\nho, app.listen() se server start karte ho. Yahan 'express' ka koi role nahi hai, sirf 'app' hi kaam kar\nraha hai.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Use karna — app object se kaam lenaapp.get(...), app.listen(...) — Ab jo object mila (app), uske andar pehle se functions maujood hain. Tum bas dot (.) lagake unko bulaate ho — jaise app.get() se route banate ho, app.listen() se server start karte ho. Yahan 'express' ka koi role nahi hai, sirf 'app' hi kaam kar raha hai.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
