      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CORS = Cross-Origin Resource Sharing\nCORS ka use Frontend aur Backend ke beech cross-origin requests ko control karne ke liye hota hai.\n\nExample:\n\nFrontend → localhost:5173\nBackend  → localhost:5000\n\nDono ke origin different hain.\n\nBrowser security ke wajah se browser check karta hai:\n\n\"Kya ye frontend backend ko request bhej sakta hai?\"\n\nCORS backend ki permission policy define karta hai.\ncors npm package Express mein CORS configuration ko easy banata hai.\n\nBasic:\n\nconst cors = require(\"cors\");\n\napp.use(cors());\n\nIska simple meaning:\n\nDifferent origin se aane wali browser requests ko allow/control karo.\n\nImportant: CORS authentication/security ka replacement nahi hai. Ye mainly browser cross-origin access control se related hai.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CORS = Cross-Origin Resource Sharing\nCORS ka use Frontend aur Backend ke beech cross-origin requests ko control karne ke liye hota hai.\n\nExample:\n\nFrontend → localhost:5173\nBackend  → localhost:5000\n\nDono ke origin different hain.\n\nBrowser security ke wajah se browser check karta hai:\n\n\"Kya ye frontend backend ko request bhej sakta hai?\"\n\nCORS backend ki permission policy define karta hai.\ncors npm package Express mein CORS configuration ko easy banata hai.\n\nBasic:\n\nconst cors = require(\"cors\");\n\napp.use(cors());\n\nIska simple meaning:\n\nDifferent origin se aane wali browser requests ko allow/control karo.\n\nImportant: CORS authentication/security ka replacement nahi hai. Ye mainly browser cross-origin access control se related hai.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jbm29xv4s4icEYnhQVO6_",
      "type": "text",
